      "path": "manuscript/latex/appendices/d-faithful-family.tex",
      "before": "\\label{cor:pair}\nLet $T\\supseteq\\PA$ be consistent.\nFix $U=\\omega$ and a Turing morphism\n$\\tau:U\\times U\\rightharpoonup U$ in $S_T$.\nChoose an isomorphism $b_0:U\\to U+U$ in $S_{\\PA}$ and put\n$b=Q_{\\PA,T}(b_0)$. Define\n\\[\n d=\\tau\\Delta_U,\\qquad\n a_0=(bd)^*(1_U+0_U),\\qquad a_1=(bd)^*(0_U+1_U).\n\\]\nThen $a_0,a_1$ are inseparable in $S_T$. For every consistent\nextension $T'\\supseteq T$, their images under $Q_{T,T'}$ are the\nidentically defined inseparable pair in $S_{T'}$.\n",
      "after": "\\label{cor:pair}\nLet $T\\supseteq\\PA$ be consistent.\nFix $U=\\omega$ and a Turing morphism\n$\\tau:U\\times U\\rightharpoonup U$ in $S_T$.\nChoose an isomorphism $b_0:U\\to U+U$ in $S_{\\PA}$ and put\n$b=Q_{\\PA,T}(b_0)$. Define\n\\[\n d=\\tau\\Delta_U,\\qquad\n a_0=(bd)^*(1_U+0_U),\\qquad a_1=(bd)^*(0_U+1_U).\n\\]\nThen $a_0,a_1$ are inseparable in $S_T$. For every consistent\nextension $T'\\supseteq T$, their images under $Q_{T,T'}$ form the\ninseparable pair defined by the same formulas in $S_{T'}$.\n"
